  "question": {
    "text": "The two light beams having intensities <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mi>I</mi></math> interfere to produce a fringe pattern on a screen. The phase difference between the beams is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;at point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#960;</mi></math> at point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math>. Then the difference between the resultant intensities at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math> will be :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "4CRlK",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>I</mi></math>",
